PCI: size bridge windows for child alignment padding

Adapted from the linux-7.0 version: on 6.8, `size += max(r_size, align)`
sits after the alignment-order check in pbus_size_mem(), not immediately
after `r_size = resource_size(r)`.

--- a/drivers/pci/setup-bus.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/setup-bus.c
@@ -1054,7 +1054,16 @@
 				r->flags = 0;
 				continue;
 			}
-			size += max(r_size, align);
+
+			/*
+			 * Every child must start at an aligned address, so a
+			 * child whose size is not a multiple of its alignment
+			 * leaves a gap before the next one. Round up so that
+			 * padding is included; this is identical to
+			 * max(r_size, align) whenever r_size <= align, which
+			 * covers ordinary device BARs where size == alignment.
+			 */
+			size += ALIGN(r_size, align);
 			/*
 			 * Exclude ranges with size > align from calculation of
 			 * the alignment.
